*======================================================================
* wovl.a99 - the workbench's overlays 5 on (M5 parts 5 and 6), assembled
* apart from wbench.a99: the first assembly's staging room (>4000->9FFF)
* holds overlays 1-4 and little more.  tools/build.py assembles wbench.a99
* first, writes its symbols (but the overlays' own labels, >B000->CFFF)
* into src/gen/wres.a99, then assembles this file with them; these
* overlays are staged from >0000 here (this assembly has nothing else) and
* go into their SAMS pages like the others.
*
* Each overlay runs at >B000 and begins there with a branch to its entry:
* the resident part calls OVENT after OVSEL.  Overlays never refer to
* each other's labels (the other is not mapped in).
*======================================================================
       COPY "macros.a99"
       COPY "gen/wres.a99"

       AORG >0000
       XORG >B000
       B    @GEN5              overlay 5: the code generator
       COPY "wcode.a99"
       COPY "gen/bops.a99"
OV5END
       XORG >B000
       B    @LINK6             overlay 6: the linker, first half
       COPY "wlink.a99"
OV6END
       XORG >B000
       B    @LINK7             overlay 7: the linker, second half
       COPY "wlink2.a99"
OV7END
       END
